      "reasoning": "All 16 mathematical answers agree with their own captured worked solutions. The source error is an introductory typo in q-51054: it says to check continuity at x=2, although the question and subsequent calculations concern x=-1. This does not change its correct answer. Independently: q-120808 factors as tan(theta)sin(theta)sec²(theta)=tan²(theta)sec(theta)=(sec²(theta)-1)sec(theta). q-114060 has f''>0 precisely on (-1,0) and (0,1), separated by the undefined point at 0. q-60145 completes to 20(x-3/2)²=4, giving q=4 and x=3/2±sqrt(5)/5. q-86414 completes to 3(x-6)²=14, so p=-6 and q-p=20. q-49332 has integrand -csc²(x), whose antiderivative is cot(x), giving -sqrt(3)/3. q-18603 subtracts the graph slopes: 0-1=-1. q-105502 uses the product rule: 1·0+(-2)·3=-6. q-1393 gives u×v=(10,-2,30); the source's basis-vector expression is equivalent. q-113763 has f'=3(x+1)², positive on both sides of its only stationary point, so there are no local extrema. q-10832 has slope -13 at (1,3), yielding y=-13x+16. q-141116 requires 1/A=1/2, so A=2. q-73457 gives b×c=(-3,-3,-3) and dot product -3+9-6=0. q-20054 gives b×c=(-12,2,8) and dot product -12-2+16=2. q-20059 divides out 9sqrt(2), then uses cyclic invariance of the scalar triple product to obtain 2. q-18658 gives a·(b×c)=-3; swapping a and b gives 3. q-51054 has left limit -2 and right limit 2, so the unequal one-sided limits cause a jump discontinuity. No submitted grades were supplied; all MA answer evidence below comes from the captured worked solutions.",
